  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many users I've met dislike the fact they trigger custom hand animations by accident, and want a way around this without outright turning them off. \n\nProposed solution (Oculus/Index): By default, the normally unused X/A (or just A on Index) buttons, when held while gesturing, bypass all avatar-specific overrides and use the VRC default hand gestures instead, until the button is released. In addition, a new Settings option called \"Bypass Gesture Overrides\" allows you to reverse this functionality and turn custom animations OFF by default, requiring you to hold the button while gesturing to activate the custom overrides.\n\nProposed solution (Vive): Uncertain as of yet, no buttons to work with. Bypass Gesture Overrides would still disable custom animations entirely for Vive users.",
